Range:

Currently, I'm playing a Monk, who only has proficiencies in Shuriken
and crossbow.  All other ranged weapons are restricted.

Well, I've tried one thing and then another, and after 6 monks I've
come to the conclusion that nothing, just nothing, beats a stack of
daggers. I find I have more luck, even unskilled, using daggers than I
do trying to find the weapons I'm technically skilled with.

After all 1) there's only one type of crossbow ammunition (the crossbow
bolt), and while it's reasonably common, it's still not as readily
available as the dagger, which comes in many varieties (crude, elvish,
silver, human) and each variety is as common as dirt.  2) Daggers,
unlike bolts or arrows, never break.  Or at least almost never.  So I
can rustproof and enchang them and be sure I'm not going to lose them
due to breakage. 3) The to-hit and damage penalties make far less of a
difference once you start climbing the experience charts.   When the
common weapons stop being effective you just charge 'em to +5 and
suddenly they're lethal again.

So:  I swear by daggers.   If the real world was like nethack, every
soldier would go into battle carrying a bandolier of the things and no
other weapon.

Melee:

Chaotic:  What? You mean you're not carrying Stormbringer?  Than why
are you still here?  Get it!

Neutral:  Any double-damage weapon.  I prefer Grayswandir despite the
shock it gives me every time I wield it because A) it doesn't hurt that
much at high levels B)  it does double damage to everything C)
moreover, it adds silver damage to boot .

In any case,  I rarely exercise any weapon outside of long sword,
because every slot spent on something else is one more slot I don't
have for the weapons I really want.

Good luck!

